# 11. Separate breach of contract from negligence

This could materially improve the legal theory.

Instead of one broad allegation:

> "BitMEX negligently failed to provide a functioning exchange."

consider three separate questions for counsel:

### Contract

What did the March 2020 Terms actually promise concerning access, trading functionality, liquidation and platform availability?

### Negligence / operational conduct

Once BitMEX knew customers were materially unable to reach their leveraged positions, did it reasonably respond to that condition?

### Causation

Can this particular trader demonstrate that he attempted—or had a realistic opportunity—to take a specific action that would have avoided or reduced liquidation?

That last piece is especially important because the federal BitMEX litigation shows that courts may be skeptical of generalized economic-loss negligence theories. ([Justia Law][5])

