# 13. Ask whether BitMEX had an SLA or internal availability target

This could be extremely interesting discovery.

Even if BitMEX gave customers **no contractual uptime guarantee**, internally it may have maintained:

* uptime targets;
* availability SLAs;
* latency thresholds;
* maximum acceptable order delay;
* API availability targets;
* authentication availability targets;
* recovery-time objectives;
* recovery-point objectives;
* severity classifications;
* incident escalation thresholds.

If BitMEX's internal standard said, for example:

> **Critical trading functionality must have 99.99% availability**

or

> **SEV-1 incident requires market suspension**

that could be much more useful than a generic external industry standard.

Ask for those records.

